tosis, or other infective findings", "Inborn errors of metabolism affecting bowel function: unlikely given uncomplicated pregnancy and absence of metabolic derangements in newborn"], "alarm_features": ["Down syndrome features (upslanting palpebral fissures, epicanthal folds, single transverse palmar crease)", "Abdominal distension with hypoactive bowel sounds in a neonate with vomiting"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Congenital Structural Obstruction of the Digestive System", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.3070175438596492, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Digital rectal exam evacuating stool and flatulence suggests partial bowel continuity, but does not definitively exclude structural obstruction due to variable presentation patterns."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Does the abdominal radiograph show a 'double-bubble' sign or intestinal gas pattern consistent with proximal obstruction?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Upper gastrointestinal contrast study", "Abdominal ultrasound for pyloric thickness"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.65, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Motility/Neurogenic Disorders Affecting Bowel Function", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.3157894736842106, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Down syndrome features (upslanting palpebral fissures, epicanthal folds, single palmar crease) significantly increase suspicion of syndromic/structural bowel abnormalities and Hirschsprung disease."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of family history reduces but does no